#: {{usex|en|I '''got''' go Taiwan next year.|I’m already/actually going to Taiwan next year.|inline=1}}
# {{senseid|en|done}} {{lb|en|Singlish|auxiliary}} {{n-g|Used to emphasize that an action has been done.}}
#: {{usex|en|I '''got''' tell them just now.|inline=1}}
# {{senseid|en|habitual}} {{lb|en|Singlish|auxiliary}} {{n-g|Marks the [[habitual aspect]] in the present or past tense}}.
#: {{usex|en|I '''got''' cook meals for them.|I cook meals for them; I would cook meals for them (now and then or regularly).|inline=1}}
#: {{usex|en|You '''got''' play badminton?|Do you play badminton?|inline=1}}

